/* book exam traps: Flat magnitude is not enough. Many answers check |H| = K and stop; a nonlinear phase still distorts the waveform, so both conditions must be checked. | Sign of the phase. A delay gives ∠H = −ω td. Writing +ω td describes an advance, which is noncausal and shifts the signal the wrong way. | Phase delay and group delay are equal only for linear phase. For any other phase they differ, so quoting one when the other is asked loses marks. | Ideal filters are not 'costly but buildable'. No amount of hardware makes them causal; the exact brick wall violates the Paley–Wiener condition. | Distortionless does not mean unity gain. K may be 0.1 or 50; only the flatness of |H| and the linearity of ∠H decide it. */
