/* book exam traps: Autocorrelation is not convolution with itself: Rx(τ)=x(τ)*x(−τ). Using x(τ)*x(τ) gives a different, non-even function. | For a power signal, Rx(0) is average power, not total energy. Total energy is infinite; do not write E=Rx(0). | Wiener–Khinchin uses |X(ω)|², not X(ω). The spectral density has no phase information. | Rxy(τ)=Ryx(−τ). Reversing the order without reversing the lag gives the wrong delay sign. | A peak in cross-correlation is at the lag that aligns the signals; do not read the peak height as the delay. Peak height measures similarity, not time. */
